>>How do I open a chest?  
> You *loot* it. If the lid opens and then closes when you kick it, it
> is unlocked, and then you use the #loot command to put things into it
> or take things out of it.
> 
> If the chest is locked, then kicking it can break the lock (but also
> risks breaking breakable things inside it: such as potions, eggs, and
> items made of glass.)

*AND* items made of crystal, which can be very very sad for spellcasters 
in need of good armour (but far away from the castle and its Nice Item).

I find that the best way to open a chest is to equip an expendable, 
non-cursed cutting weapon (such as a dagger), stand on it and #force the 
lock. There is a chance that this will break the weapon, so only use 
weapons you don't mind losing.

Oh, and don't use a blunt weapon to #force a chest - unless you really 
are role-playing a stereotyped barbarian...

